cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
title: "Actionable DMP: a data management plan a machine can check"
abstract: >-
  A static, client-side web tool and command-line checker for machine-actionable data
  management plans. It turns the six core requirements and fifteen questions of Science
  Europe's Practical Guide to the International Alignment of Research Data Management (2021)
  into dmp.json, a plan that validates against the RDA DMP Common Standard v1.2, and checks
  what the plan says about each dataset (DOI, access, licence, repository, formats, grant)
  against the dataset's DOI record at DataCite, in the browser, on the command line, or as a
  GitHub Action. Code under MIT; schema, examples and texts under CC BY 4.0.
